  <div class="answer-box">
    <p>Chicken jerky is safe for dogs when it is <strong>plain chicken breast and nothing else</strong>. Trim the fat, slice 1/4 inch thick, heat the strips to <strong>165°F</strong>, then dry at 160°F for 4–6 hours. Never use a human jerky marinade — garlic and onion are toxic to dogs and the sodium is far too high.</p>
